@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-1 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": `cargo smysl hooks install` writes a post-commit hook that appends the sha to `.smysl/queue` and nothing else. }
~ `cargo smysl hooks install` writes a post-commit hook that appends the sha to `.smysl/queue` and nothing else.

To ensure extraction is done at a moment chosen by a person, without failing a commit or taking time during the commit process.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-2 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The same command registers `*.smy merge=smysl` in .gitattributes, and prints the one `git config` line git requires per clone." }
~ The same command registers `*.smy merge=smysl` in .gitattributes, and prints the one `git config` line git …

To enable smysl's own merge driver for handling corpus document merges without user intervention.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-3 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "A test caught the driver accepting a file it understood nothing of and overwriting it with an empty document. Text that yields no records is now refused, and git is told the merge failed." }
~ A test caught the driver accepting a file it understood nothing of and overwriting it with an empty document. …

To prevent a silent overwrite of someone's file by a merge driver that does not understand the content.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-4 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": ".smysl/commits/` and `.smysl/bench/` are tracked: the record, and a person's labels." }
~ .smysl/commits/` and `.smysl/bench/` are tracked: the record, and a person's labels.

To ensure that the record and a person's labels are preserved across clones and not lost during extraction or other operations.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-5 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b2dbe4820872.smy@4b6a6cfe6057 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Add `cargo-smysl-facts` as a dependency }
~ Add `cargo-smysl-facts` as a dependency.

To support the retrieval and matching of facts, which is part of the verdict stage.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-6 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b2dbe4820872.smy@4b6a6cfe6057 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Add `matching` module to `lib.rs` }
~ Add `matching` module to `lib.rs`.

To handle the checking of one claim against the facts, as part of the matching process.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-7 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b2dbe4820872.smy@4b6a6cfe6057 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Update `Cargo.toml` with new dependencies and features }
