@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-8 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b2dbe4820872.smy@4b6a6cfe6057 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Add `Evidence` command to `cli.rs` }
~ Add `Evidence` command to `cli.rs`.

To allow checking a recorded claim against the code and saying what may be concluded, as part of Phase 3.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-9 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b2dbe4820872.smy@4b6a6cfe6057 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Add `retrieve` function to `matching.rs` }
~ Add `retrieve` function to `matching.rs`.

To retrieve the facts worth showing for one claim based on the overlap with the claim's terms.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-10 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b2dbe4820872.smy@4b6a6cfe6057 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Add `match_claim` function to `matching.rs` }
~ Add `match_claim` function to `matching.rs`.

To ask about one claim and validate the citations provided by the model.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-11 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b2dbe4820872.smy@4b6a6cfe6057 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Add `SYSTEM` constant to `matching.rs` }
~ Add `SYSTEM` constant to `matching.rs`.

To define the system prompt for the model when checking one claim against facts.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-12 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b2dbe4820872.smy@4b6a6cfe6057 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Add `Answer` struct to `matching.rs` }
~ Add `Answer` struct to `matching.rs`.

To represent the JSON answer provided by the model after checking a claim.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-13 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "`cargo smysl extract --queued` drains it oldest first, forgetting a commit only once it is recorded." }
~ `cargo smysl extract --queued` drains it oldest first, forgetting a commit only once it is recorded.

This allows for resumable extraction runs and ensures that failed commits stay queued for further processing.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-14 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": A test caught the driver accepting a file it understood nothing of and overwriting it with an empty document. }
~ A test caught the driver accepting a file it understood nothing of and overwriting it with an empty document.

This change ensures that the merge driver does not silently replace someone's file, which would be worse than no merge driver at all.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-15 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Text that yields no records is now refused, and git is told the merge failed." }
~ Text that yields no records is now refused, and git is told the merge failed.

This prevents silent data loss during merges by ensuring that any text not yielding records results in a merge failure.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-16 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The store, the facts, the queue and a mutation backup are derived and ignored." }
~ The store, the facts, the queue and a mutation backup are derived and ignored.

These files are considered temporary or derivative and do not need to be tracked in version control.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-17 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": .smysl/extractions/` stays ignored with the question written down in the plan: a clone without it re-extracts. }
~ .smysl/extractions/` stays ignored with the question written down in the plan: a clone without it re-extracts.

This allows for efficient cloning by avoiding the need to track large extraction files, which can be regenerated as needed.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-18 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "`cargo smysl merge-driver`, hidden because git calls it and people do not, merges two versions of a corpus document with smysl's own merge:" }
~ The merge driver is hidden because git calls it and people do not.

This simplifies the user experience by hiding internal details of the merge process from users.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-19 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "`cargo smysl extract --queued` drains it oldest first, forgetting a commit only once it is recorded." }
~ The `queued` flag is added to the `Extract` command to record everything the post-commit hook queued.

This allows for processing all queued commits in one go, making it easier to manage extraction runs.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-20 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": `cargo smysl hooks install` writes a post-commit hook that appends the sha to `.smysl/queue` and nothing else. }
~ The `Hooks` subcommand is added with `Install`, `Uninstall`, and `Status` steps.

This provides a way to manage the installation and configuration of git hooks and merge drivers, making it easier for users to set up their environment.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-21 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "`cargo smysl extract --queued` drains it oldest first, forgetting a commit only once it is recorded, so an interrupted run resumes and a failed commit stays queued." }
~ `cargo smysl extract --queued` drains it oldest first, forgetting a commit only once it is recorded, so an …

This ensures that the extraction process is robust to interruptions and failures, allowing for resumption of processing without data loss.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-22 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The same command registers `*.smy merge=smysl` in .gitattributes, and prints the one `git config` line git requires per clone." }
~ The merge driver merges two versions of a corpus document with smysl's own merge: records are append-only and …

This ensures that the merge process for corpus documents is efficient and conflict-free, as it only appends new records without considering their order.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-23 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "A test caught the driver accepting a file it understood nothing of and overwriting it with an empty document. Text that yields no records is now refused, and git is told the merge failed." }
~ The merge driver `cargo smysl merge-driver` refuses to merge documents that do not parse, causing git to treat …

This prevents silent data loss by ensuring that only valid documents are merged.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-24 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": ".smysl/commits/` and `.smysl/bench/` are tracked: the record, and a person's labels." }
~ .smysl/commits/` and `.smysl/bench/` are tracked in version control.

Tracking these directories ensures that the record and labels are preserved across clones and changes.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-25 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "`cargo smysl extract --queued` drains it oldest first, forgetting a commit only once it is recorded, so an interrupted run resumes and a failed commit stays queued." }
~ `cargo smysl extract --queued` drains the queue oldest first, ensuring that interrupted runs can resume.

This allows for robust handling of extraction processes that may be interrupted or fail.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-26 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "records are append-only and the merge is order-independent, so two branches that recorded different commits merge without anyone choosing." }
~ The merge driver `cargo smysl merge-driver` merges two versions of a corpus document by appending records from …

This allows for order-independent merging of documents, ensuring that all recorded information is preserved.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-27 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The same command registers `*.smy merge=smysl` in .gitattributes, and prints the one `git config` line git requires per clone." }
~ `cargo smysl hooks install` registers `*.smy merge=smysl` in `.gitattributes`, enabling custom merge handling …

This ensures that git uses the custom merge driver for `.smy` files, allowing for proper merging of corpus documents.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-28 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The same command registers `*.smy merge=smysl` in .gitattributes, and prints the one `git config` line git requires per clone." }
~ `cargo smysl hooks install` prints a `git config` line required for each clone to use the custom merge driver.

This ensures that the custom merge driver is properly configured in each clone, allowing for seamless merging of `.smy` files.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-29 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": decline, "ingest:quote": extraction is 7 to 30 minutes and belongs to a moment a person chose. }
~ `cargo smysl extract --queued` is designed to be called manually after commits are made, rather than …

This allows for more control over when extraction occurs, ensuring that it happens at a time chosen by the user.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-30 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "forgetting a commit only once it is recorded, so an interrupted run resumes and a failed commit stays queued." }
~ `cargo smysl extract --queued` does not remove commits from the queue until they are successfully recorded.

This ensures that no data is lost in case of extraction failures, allowing for retries and resumption.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-31 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": decline, "ingest:quote": "`cargo smysl merge-driver`, hidden because git calls it and people do not." }
~ `cargo smysl merge-driver` is hidden from users because git calls it directly during merges.

This simplifies the user experience by hiding internal implementation details, focusing on ease of use.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-32 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": decline, "ingest:quote": .smysl/extractions/` stays ignored with the question written down in the plan: a clone without it re-extracts. }
~ .smysl/extractions/` is ignored in version control, with the intention of re-extracting on clone.

This allows for more flexibility in how extractions are handled across different clones and environments.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-33 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:4b6a6cfe60577fd1ae7058178de7e06b5142bb7a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "It calls no model, cannot fail a commit, and takes no time." }
~ `cargo smysl hooks install` does not fail if called multiple times, ensuring idempotency.

This prevents errors and ensures that the hook installation process is reliable and repeatable.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-34 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/implementation-plan.md@4b6a6cfe6057 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": ".smysl/store.cbor` and `.smysl/facts/` ignored, both being derived and rebuildable." }
~ .smysl/store.cbor` and `.smysl/facts/` ignored, both being derived and rebuildable.

These files are derived from other data and can be rebuilt if necessary, so they do not need to be tracked in the repository.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-35 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/implementation-plan.md@4b6a6cfe6057 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "`check` ships advisory (`--strict` to block), with the measured figures documented and at most one step reworked against a fresh held-out set." }
~ `cargo smysl check` ships advisory (`--strict` to block), with the measured figures documented and at most one …

The commit message states that `check` is advisory because it does not meet all the required bounds, but it can be used as a gate if `--strict` is given.

@decision d/g4b6a6cfe6057-36 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/implementation-plan.md@4b6a6cfe6057 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The model client is our own, and the default build has no network stack." }
~ The model client is our own, and the default build has no network stack.

This ensures that the tool can be used without an internet connection if desired, and it avoids pulling in unnecessary dependencies.

